coi doi djek

I really like your sample speech, and I'm looking forward to seeing what you
come up with next!  

Incedentally, and not to belittle your TTS accomplishment, where do you
live?  Did you record the sound bits used in the construction of the sample
speech?  If I assume from your email address that you live in the southern
US, that might explain the noticible southern twang your sample speech
exhibits. Not that this is bad, I expect it falls well within the acceptable
lojban pronunciation limits.  It's just something I hadn't expected at all,
and I found it rather amusing to hear a computer speaking to me in lojban
with a southern accent.  My whole family's from Arkansas, and I find myself
picking up the accent myself every time I visit them for more than a day or
two.  I live in the Baltimore, Maryland area, btw.

